From ee0bb0be54c19083636ada6df0509079c4f86ec7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gareth Davidson <gaz@bitplane.net>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 16:57:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] Lower TempleOS kernel intrinsics

Provide the integer, memory, queue and CPU operations used by the kernel. Track scratch registers and preserve operands across calls; reject x86-only operations on other targets.

Include focused checks for queue mutation, string length, swaps and unsigned remainder. Privileged operations are compiled but are not executed in the host regression tests.
